= Prosh Proshian

Proshian (1883-1918), a Left SR, is a telegraph man, with a network of operators who are loyal to the party.

**Telegraph Lines.** Proshian's telegraph network carries news and the party's organisation.

*Effect:* Support among workers +1, railwaymen +2; +8,000 members; the village organisers: strength +1, dissent −2; better intelligence for the Vikzhel talks on an all-socialist government (November 1917).

*Calling on an advisor takes the turn, and then no advisor can act again for six months.*

- @action
- @root: Return to main

@action
title: Telegraph Lines
subtitle: Proshian's telegraph network carries news and the party's organisation. Support among workers +1, railwaymen +2; +8,000 members; the village organisers: strength +1, dissent −2; better intelligence for the Vikzhel talks on an all-socialist government (November 1917).
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0 and lsr_in_gov = 1 and mem_full = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [? if advisor_action_timer > 1 : [+ advisor_wait +] months before the next advisor action. ?][? if advisor_action_timer > 0 and advisor_action_timer <= 1 : One month before the next advisor action. ?][? if not (lsr_in_gov = 1) : We are not in the government. ?][? if mem_full = 1 : The party already has about as many members as its committees can organise. ?]
on-arrival: {!
Q.advisor_action_timer = 6;
Q.last_advisor_action = 1;
Q.month_actions += 1;
Q.insight = (Q.insight || 0) + 1; Q.members += 10 * Q.mem_scale; RO.boost(Q, {workers: 1, railway: 2}); RO.fac(Q, 'unions', 1, -2);
!}

The telegraphists of a dozen provincial towns now take their instructions from the party, and the party hears everything that goes over the wire.

- @root: Continue.
